   "kind": "assistant",
   "reply": {
    "message": "I made a test-pattern show for your 240x240 colour screen. Press Apply under the animated preview to use it. Each screen lasts 3 seconds, then it loops:\n1. Colour bars\n2. Checkerboard (30 px squares, white and black)\n3. Rainbow gradient\n4. Bouncing yellow ball\n\nA small label at the bottom names each pattern. Nothing here is a sensor reading, so there are no simulated values. The preview is only a simulation. The real screen shows it after you write the code and upload it.\n\nYour wiring passed the checker with no errors or warnings. It is SCL to D18 (GPIO 18), SDA to D23 (GPIO 23), RES to D25 (GPIO 25) and DC to D26 (GPIO 26), plus 3V3 and GND. SCL and SDA here are SPI clock and data, not I2C. The BLK pin (backlight) is unconnected, which leaves the backlight on.\n\nI have not tested the real screen. The agent is not streaming, so I have no live readings. If the screen stays blank after upload, I can check the pins with you.\n\nDo you want me to write the Arduino code for this test-pattern show?",
